  "description": "Throughout all elevations:\n•\tTo replace the existing single-glazed timber-sash windows with bespoke double-glazed and argon filled timber sash windows designed like for like by a specialist\n•\tRepair and repoint the London stock brick, especially at the rear where sub-standard ‘patches of different brick’ have been introduced throughout the years\nAt ground floor:\n•\tA single storey rear extension of 2.1 meters, limited to the host building only \n•\tTo replace the existing conservatory with a new construction built with cavity-walls\n•\tTo extend the rear terrace as hard paving by 1.9m the full width of the house\n\nAt loft /roof level:\n•\tTo insert two rooflights to the front roof slope within a conservation-style flush fitted frame, symmetrically placed on the main roof\n•\tTo insert a new non-openable skylight on the existing flat roof on the rear outrigger of the house\n•\tTo insert one roof light to the side roof slope within a conservation-style flush fitted frame",
